  "terrainName": "basic-desert",
  "description": "What: CE-4650 (NA-4, R-4281 fun pack) - a Native American WAR PARTY circles a guarded camp. 'War chief' commands six war ponies ('War pony 1'..'6', each a 'Warrior n' of type 2016 with a bow) assembled at the west edge of the desert; CircleRaid rides each pony to its OWN ring point round the camp at (300,330), then circles it at a gallop (ordered 40-80 m ring points; the ponies' measured path stays within about 60 m of the camp) while every warrior shoots 'Camp guard 1' from the saddle; a hit rider breaks off and rejoins; at the end they ride to the rally. The four camp guards (type 2002) are told to hold fire, so the party's arrows - not a firefight - are what is judged. Judge: warriors shoot at least six arrows while their ponies gallop, at least one arrow hits a guard, and no pony halts to let its rider shoot (ponies keep galloping)."
 },
